{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 32d69a5856a7c87565233e3cbdbdcddf5cf77cf8 (tree b1badec4caef44f9ba257487f7f68bd6b6fbf63b), the two OB-L notes on published 42d35b88. The verdict binds the OB-L implementation promise 544617ee and signs both path artifacts, with the implementation note first.\n\n## What the head records\nThe one authorized Demo observation returned no data. The note says so, states that no bound was chosen, and leaves the choice of a busier deployment or fresh selector to the planner. The design note's Status now says live calibration and full acceptance stay open, and links the result.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The two filed artifacts equal the two changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only 42d35b88 32d69a58`).\n- **Observation.** The five files in `2026-11-22-ob-l-demo-observation/` match the note's five SHA-256 values. The evaluator at 42d35b88 hashes to `a62950f0…`, as the note says. `invocation.json` reads head 42d35b88, exit 0, 1,753 ms. `observation.stdout.json` reads `eventCount` 0, `weightedRows` 0, `routeCount` 0, `turnCount` 0, `errors` 0, `errorRate` null, `routeP95Ms` null, `p95BoundMs` null, coverage `unknown`, failures `calibration`, `no-data`, `coverage`. The window runs from 09:52:35 to 10:07:35 UTC on 22 November, as the note states, and the version is 9c2c2413, the Demo version the planner deployed.\n- **Credential-free.** The standard error stream is empty. The only 40-character-or-longer string in the five files is the published head. `run-observation.mjs` refuses to write a stream that contains the token, the account identifier, an authorization header or a bearer value. The note names neither token nor account.\n- **Status limit.** `scripts/deploy-check.mjs` at 42d35b88 stops with \"missing calibration\" unless the caller supplies an integer `p95BoundMs`, and it reads a calibration record with a format, deployment, version, window, route count, p95 and bound. So the Status sentence \"requires an observed bound before it can query its first calibration window\" is true to the code.\n- **Gate.** The notes-only gate at a4d73d40 (tree 71d80a47) has `gate.txt` SHA-256 `14de247b…`, shows \"changed files 0\", ends \"gate passed\", and `gate.exit` reads 0. END act e02b1082 matches. The review head differs from a4d73d40 only in the implementation note, so no second gate applies. The ruling skips the gate for a notes-only head, so this run was extra.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (42d35b88) is clean with tree b1badec4. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 2. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings.\n\n## Wake rate\nTwo notes change. No alarm, retry or reschedule is added, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged. The observation itself made one read-only analytics query and one health read, both outside the Durable Objects.\n\n## Architecture\nThe note keeps the observation, its limits and the planner's open choice apart. It does not claim a calibrated pass or the absence of busy turns, and the evaluator's own `gaps` agree.\n\n## Security\nRead-only, bounded and credential-free, as above. The credential handling that ruling 023b7d7b set (a scratch adapter outside the checkout) is the one the note describes. Nothing in the head touches a token path, a header or a custody path.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove. The design note changes by one Status paragraph.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Home path.** The note writes the evidence directory as `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/…`. Every other note on main writes `~/play/artroom-evidence/…`, and the same note uses that form for the gate log. Change it to `~/` at the next edit of this note.\n2. **Landing order.** The planner's E5 continuation edits `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md` and these notes edit two other files, so the two heads do not overlap. Either can land first.\n3. **Scratch scripts.** The adapter and launcher live only in the evidence directory. A later head can add the adapter to the repository if the planner wants it reused. That head needs its own review.\n\nNo gate is required: the head changes only notes.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3edefd636279d4dc0020fe8d005419c1b945e2d3","binding":"assigned","head":"32d69a5856a7c87565233e3cbdbdcddf5cf77cf8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aedf788c89615bf71c116225afd284e89147c440\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:544617ee4b121489e57ecb111e72b7d3f188c489\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a67d78d8f2b6d5c9b69c31352368cf6236da79ee","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}